Given state equation is, \[\frac{d}{dt}
\left[\begin{array}{c}
x_{1}\\
x_{2}
\end{array}\right]
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 &amp; 0\\
1 &amp; 1
\end{array}\right]
\left[\begin{array}{c}
x_{1}\\
x_{2}
\end{array}\right]\] with initial condition, \[x(0)=
\left[\begin{array}{c}
1\\
0
\end{array}\right]\] Zero input response is given by, \[X(s)=[sI-A]^{-1}x(0)\] First compute, \[sI-A=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
s-1 &amp; 0\\
-1 &amp; s-1
\end{array}\right]\] Determinant is, \[|sI-A|
=
(s-1)^2\] Therefore, \[[sI-A]^{-1}
=
\frac{1}{(s-1)^2}
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
s-1 &amp; 0\\
1 &amp; s-1
\end{array}\right]\] \[=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
\dfrac{1}{s-1} &amp; 0\\ \dfrac{1}{(s-1)^2} &amp; \dfrac{1}{s-1}
\end{array}\right]\] Hence, \[X(s)
=
\left[\begin{array}{cc}
\dfrac{1}{s-1} &amp; 0\\ \dfrac{1}{(s-1)^2} &amp; \dfrac{1}{s-1}
\end{array}\right]
\left[\begin{array}{c}
1\\
0
\end{array}\right]\] \[X(s)
=
\left[\begin{array}{c}
\dfrac{1}{s-1}\\ \dfrac{1}{(s-1)^2}
\end{array}\right]\] Taking inverse Laplace transform, \[x(t)
=
\left[\begin{array}{c}
e^t\\
te^t
\end{array}\right]\] \[\boxed{\text{(C) }\begin{bmatrix}e^t\\ te^t\end{bmatrix}}\]
